{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CdsWoNZ4u12fcovYwPRAu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stage S1 is complete. All four deliverables are written in the workspace root: `distinctions.json`, `value-estimates.json`, `spec-summary.json`, and `execution-ledger.jsonl` (five node events in the mandated order, no complete event).\n\n**Distinctions (4).** The task asks for conformance verdicts on three stack-machine interpreters against `spec.md` over six programs. Q1–Q3 are the per-candidate verdicts (each hinges on a specific semantic delta: candidate A errors on POP-of-empty where the spec continues; candidate C no-ops SWAP-underflow where the spec halts with ERROR; candidate B tracks the spec closely but conformance still needs full per-program derivation). All three are locally resolvable — hard care-work, but nothing about their admissibility requires another process.\n\nQ4 is the structurally interesting one, mapping to evidence requirement E-B: a re-derivation by a disjoint method \"without consulting the first derivation's intermediate work.\" A single process that produces the first derivation cannot un-see its own traces, so I marked Q4 as not locally resolvable, requiring isolation, contaminating, capability-bearing (the worker must author inputs for a separate process), and session-spanning. This is the feature signal that should drive the downstream ranker toward a two-process family.\n\n**Value estimates.** `local` gets delta_e 0.6 — it can satisfy E-A and very likely E-C, but its E-B evidence is inadmissible by authorship, and its second-pass records are duplicative (redundancy 0.2). `isolated-child` gets the top estimate (delta_e 0.9, redundancy 0.05): a child given only the package artifacts and a prescribed disjoint method produces the cleanest admissible E-B evidence. `local-independent-verify` sits just below (0.85) because the examiner sees the answers, which satisfies E-B's letter but carries some anchoring risk. `branching` is discounted slightly from isolated-child (0.85) for the chance the run-time chooser picks the wrong branch. Governance risk is 0.0 across the board — I have no concrete expectation of a formal failure under the deterministic machinery."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1782,"cache_read_input_tokens":47618,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1782},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e5a4cb7c-0fa6-4d91-ac22-d6560b2742f1","uuid":"14c90c6b-bcc6-4ab4-9a3e-9f2f63eda436","timestamp":"2026-08-09T16:47:09.794Z","request_id":"req_011CdsWoLhwrgi68YscNkRek"}
